<article class="env-corollary" id="23E4EE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/23E4EE">Corollary <span data-tag="23E4EE">8.2.6.12</span>.</a> Let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calC '$ be a functor between presentable categories which preserves filtered colimits, and let $W_{\calC '}$ be a perfect class of morphisms in $\calC '$. Then $W_{\calC } = F^{-1} W_{\calC '}$ is a perfect class of morphisms in $\calC $. </p>
